From 2a3db47911f31a9b2c35a4e2b94d9d4e5c1c6d24 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin Michaud <jmichaud@igalia.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 10:19:57 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 21/23] [mya] Add `heap` and `heapdump` commands Need the bug
 URL (OOPS!).

Reviewed by NOBODY (OOPS!).

`heap [<vm>]` walks the JS heap of the current snapshot from the VM at <vm>
or, without one, from WebCore's g_commonVMOrNull or else JSC's
VMManager::s_recentVM, and reports: the live cells, what share of libpas's
allocations the walk reaches and reads as a type, the cells read as their
class, why values were not followed, the bytes missed by cause and the
largest misses with what holds them, the most untyped allocations, and the
time each phase took. It says whether the target was at mya's safe point,
and so whether the numbers are exact.

`heapdump <file> [<vm>]` writes the walk as a GCDebugging heap snapshot that
Web Inspector opens, and summarizes what it wrote (and on Darwin how it
relates to libpas's footprint).

JavaScriptCore's image is found among the snapshot's images by name
(JavaScriptCore.framework, libJavaScriptCore.so, libjavascriptcore*).

* Source/JavaScriptCore/mya/mya.cpp:

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
